{
  "slug": "spec-writing",
  "concept": "Spec Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "An engineering spec is a contract. It says WHAT a system, component, endpoint, or message must do — independent of HOW it is implemented.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "An engineering spec is a contract. It says WHAT a system, component, endpoint, or message must do - independent of HOW it is implemented.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Three forms dominate modern practice:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "API specs - machine-readable contracts for HTTP (OpenAPI 3.1) and event-driven (AsyncAPI 3.0) interfaces",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Behavior specs - executable narratives (Gherkin / Given-When-Then)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Data specs - schema contracts (JSON Schema, Avro, Protobuf)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Joel Spolsky's 2000 series \"Painless Functional Specifications\" introduced the discipline: a functional spec describes how a product works from the user's perspective; a technical spec describes internal implementation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. Spec says WHAT, not HOW",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A spec that says \"internally we'll use a Redis cache with 5-minute TTL\" has leaked implementation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#1-spec-says-what-not-how",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Litmus test: If you could swap out the implementation entirely and the spec still holds, the spec is at the right level.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#1-spec-says-what-not-how",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Contract-first design",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Contract-first development: agree on the contract before writing code. The OpenAPI / AsyncAPI document is the source of truth.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#2-contract-first-design",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. OpenAPI 3.1 for HTTP APIs",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Key top-level fields:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#3-openapi-31-for-http-apis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "openapi - version (3.1.0)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#3-openapi-31-for-http-apis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "info - name, version, description",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#3-openapi-31-for-http-apis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "servers - base URLs per environment",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#3-openapi-31-for-http-apis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "paths - endpoints, verbs, parameters, request/response shapes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#3-openapi-31-for-http-apis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "components - reusable schemas, parameters, responses, security schemes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#3-openapi-31-for-http-apis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "YAML is preferred over JSON for human authoring.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#3-openapi-31-for-http-apis",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. AsyncAPI 3.0 for events",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Key concepts in v3.0:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#4-asyncapi-30-for-events",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Channels are addressable destinations (Kafka topic, AMQP queue) - decoupled from operations",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#4-asyncapi-30-for-events",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Operations describe what an application does on a channel using action: send or action: receive",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#4-asyncapi-30-for-events",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Messages are defined once and referenced from channels and operations",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#4-asyncapi-30-for-events",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Gherkin / Given-When-Then for behavior specs",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use Gherkin for: business-logic behavior (pricing rules, eligibility checks, state transitions), workflows spanning multiple systems.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#5-gherkin-given-when-then-for-behavior-specs",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Avoid Gherkin for: API shape (use OpenAPI), data format (use JSON Schema).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#5-gherkin-given-when-then-for-behavior-specs",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Spec-as-contract mindset",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A spec is a promise. Once published:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#6-spec-as-contract-mindset",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Versioning - non-breaking changes bump minor; breaking changes bump major.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#6-spec-as-contract-mindset",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Backward compatibility - additive changes (new optional field) are safe; removals, renames, type changes are breaking.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#6-spec-as-contract-mindset",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Deprecation policy - published timeline (e.g., 12 months notice for major version sunset).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#6-spec-as-contract-mindset",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Versioning conventions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "URL versioning (/v1/users) - explicit, cacheable",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#7-versioning-conventions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Date-pinned versioning (Stripe: Stripe-Version: 2024-04-10) - fine-grained",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#7-versioning-conventions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Version in the topic name (orders.v1, orders.v2)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#7-versioning-conventions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Schema registry with explicit compatibility modes (BACKWARD, FORWARD, FULL)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#7-versioning-conventions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Examples are part of the spec",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "OpenAPI's examples field and Gherkin's Examples: table are not decorative - they are the spec. CI tools validate that examples conform to the declared schema.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#8-examples-are-part-of-the-spec",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Implementation leakage - spec mentions Redis, Postgres, language choice.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No examples - schemas without concrete payloads.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Hand-waved errors - \"returns an error on failure\" without listing codes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Missing versioning policy.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Spec-test drift - spec says one thing, implementation does another, no CI check.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Optional everything - every field is optional, every status code is default.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/spec-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
